---
import Doc from '../layouts/Doc.astro';
import SiteLink from '../components/SiteLink.astro';
import { APP_NAME, BUSINESS_NAME, SUPPORT_EMAIL } from '../utils/env';

const effectiveDateISO = '2026-08-29';
const effectiveDateLabel = 'August 29, 2026';
---

<Doc
  title="Privacy"
  description={`How ${APP_NAME} handles data.`}
>
  <header class="doc__header">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
  </header>

  <p>{APP_NAME} is published by {BUSINESS_NAME}.</p>

  <section>
    <h2>Analytics</h2>
    <p>
      {APP_NAME} sends data to <SiteLink href="https://telemetrydeck.com/privacy/" target="_blank" aria-label="TelemetryDeck privacy policy, opens in new tab">TelemetryDeck</SiteLink> to help improve the app. It includes app
      use, purchases, crashes, performance, app and device details, device
      settings, and a random ID for each install.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics can be disabled in the app's settings. Data already sent is kept
      with no set deletion date. It has no name or email, so a person's records
      cannot be found or deleted.
    </p>
    <p>
      TelemetryDeck must protect the data as required by this policy and Apple's
      privacy rules.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Content reports</h2>
    <p>
      Content reports are sent by email. They include game data, the sender's
      email address, and any attached drawing. They are used to review reported
      content.
    </p>
    <p>
      Report emails are kept in the support inbox. To delete one, email <SiteLink href={`mailto:${SUPPORT_EMAIL}`}>{SUPPORT_EMAIL}</SiteLink> from the address that sent it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Tracking</h2>
    <p>
      No one uses {APP_NAME} to track activity on other websites or in other
      companies' apps.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>Important changes to this policy are posted here.</p>
  </section>

  <footer class="doc__meta">Effective <time datetime={effectiveDateISO}>{effectiveDateLabel}</time>.</footer>
</Doc>
